<div>
 <h2 class="section-title">What to send with a referral</h2>
 <p>Sending these together is what keeps a referral from stalling at intake. If something is missing we chase it ourselves and tell your office what we needed — we don't send the referral back.</p>
 <div class="grid grid--2 mt-6">
  <div class="card card--soft">
   <h3>Always</h3>
   <ul>
    <li>Signed prescriber order — drug, dose, route, frequency, and duration</li>
    <li>Diagnosis with ICD-10 code</li>
    <li>Patient name, date of birth, address, and phone number</li>
    <li>Insurance information — plan and member ID, or a copy of the card</li>
    <li>Referring prescriber, NPI, and the best contact at your office</li>
   </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card card--soft">
   <h3>Send it if you have it</h3>
   <ul>
    <li>Recent clinical notes supporting medical necessity</li>
    <li>Recent labs relevant to the prescribed therapy</li>
    <li>Height and weight, for weight-based dosing</li>
    <li>Allergies and current medication list</li>
    <li>Prior therapy history, if the plan requires step therapy</li>
    <li>Caregiver name and contact, where one is involved</li>
   </ul>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class="cta-row">
  <a class="btn btn--primary" href="refer.html">Refer a Patient →</a>
  <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="coreflow-fax-cover-sheet.pdf" download>Download Fax Cover Sheet →</a>
 </div>
 <p class="footnote mt-4">Fax <strong>{{ site.fax }}</strong> · Phone <strong>{{ site.phone }}</strong> · {{ site.hours }}</p>
</div>
